C/span>[t]onis\u003C/span> · par[e]n[t]es \u003Cbr id=\"al5-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>vix(it) · an(nis) · XVII·m(ensibus)·VII·d(iebus)·XX \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Timothy Smith\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>D·M·S\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[.]·\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Aelio\">AE[..]O\u003C/span>·PIO·FILIO\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Eutyches\">[.]U[.]YCH[.]S\u003C/span>·[..]·\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Coe\n                tonis\">COE\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>[.]ONIS\u003C/span>·PAR[.]N[.]ES\u003Cbr id=\"al5-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">5\u003C/span>VIX·AN·XVII·M·VII·D·XX\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>CIL\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2684-2030\">Timothy Smith\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Sacred to the gods of the underworld. Eutyches and Coetonis, his parents, [gave this] to their dutiful son, Titus Aelius. He lived for seventeen years, seven months, and twenty days.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Lacunae are rationalized by Mommsen from Ansaldi's 1851 edition. The latter rendered 'T. Aelio' as IAEIO (line 2) and 'Eutyches et Coetonis parentes' as FVIYCHIS·FICOE / IONIS PARINIES (lines 3 and 4)\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Ansaldi 1851 \u003Ca href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/buchseite/724749\" target=\"_blank\">52 no. 18\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002182\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002182\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Mommsen 1883 \u003Ca href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/buchseite/650753\" target=\"_blank\">7005\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  \u003C/div>",[175,178,181,184,187,190,193,196],{"id":176,"html":177},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Timothy Smith\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>D(is) · M(anibus) · s(acrum) \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Tito\">T(ito)\u003C/span>] · \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Aelio\">Ae[li]o\u003C/span> · pio · filio \u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Eutyches\">[E]u[t]ych[e]s\u003C/span> · [et] · \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-nam